      "slug": "gram:zehi",
      "variants": [],
      "steps_unavailable": "Invariable adverb placed BEFORE the predicate. The record's own formation states it takes no particle and does not inflect, and every combination it lists is pre-posed (ぜひ + 〜てください, ぜひ + 〜たい). The closed op enum only transforms a base and suffixes tokens to it, so no ordered step list can put ぜひ in front; encoding the 〜てください or 〜たい half would emit generic request/desire morphology carrying none of this point's own material.",
      "nuance_tags": ["emphasis", "request", "desire"],
      "usage_contexts": ["spoken", "written"]
    },
    {
      "slug": "gram:zenzen-nai",
      "variants": [],
      "steps_unavailable": "Circumfix built on a pre-predicate adverb. The record is precise (全然 stands before the verb, adjective or copula and that predicate goes negative: 〜ない / 〜ません / 〜くない / 〜じゃない), but the closed op set has append and no prepend, so the 全然 slot cannot be produced by an ordered build sequence. Steps covering only the negative half would emit 書かない as if it were the pattern.",
      "nuance_tags": ["emphasis"],
      "usage_contexts": ["spoken", "written"]
