      "slug": "gram:n3-ba-hodo",
      "variants": [],
      "steps_unavailable": "The pattern requires the SAME lexical item twice: its conditional-ば form followed by its own plain/attributive form + ほど (書けば書くほど, 高ければ高いほど). The op enum builds one surface by transforming a single base and appending literal tokens; it has no operation that re-emits the base, and an append token is a fixed string, so no ordered sequence can generate the second copy. Emitting only [to-conditional-ba] would produce 高ければ, which is the plain ば conditional (a separate point), not this pattern.",
      "nuance_tags": ["comparison"],
      "usage_contexts": ["spoken", "written"]
    },
    {
      "slug": "gram:n3-ba-noni",
      "variants": [],
      "steps_unavailable": "Two-clause frame, not a derivation from one base. Per the record's own formation the ば conditional sits on clause 1 while のに closes an independent clause 2 (usually in the past). A step list transforms exactly one base, so any sequence here would either stop at 行けば, which is the plain ば conditional and a separate point, or suffix のに straight onto the conditional and license the ungrammatical *行けばのに.",
      "nuance_tags": ["desire", "condition"],
      "usage_contexts": ["spoken", "written"]
    },
