      "slug": "gram:n3-dake-shika",
      "variants": [],
      "steps_unavailable": "Discontinuous two-site pattern. だけしか attaches to a noun or a quantity, but the obligatory negation lands on a DIFFERENT word, the predicate verb (カレーだけしか食べない, 5人だけしか招待しなかった). The op set appends to one base only and cannot force the negative onto the separate predicate, so a step list of the shape [noun, append だけしか] would license the ungrammatical *カレーだけしか食べる, which is the error the record's own nuance field names as the most common one here.",
      "nuance_tags": ["emphasis"],
      "usage_contexts": ["spoken", "written"]
    },
